<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Bakhtiari confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1934 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A great confederation of Lur nomadic tribes in the Zagros whose khans grew rich from oil and helped win Iran's constitutional revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lurs">Lur</a> tribes who migrate between winter pastures in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> and summer pastures in the high <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a>. By the 18th century they were organised into two main divisions, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haft-lang">Haft Lang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chahar-lang">Chahar Lang</a>, under khans who supplied troops to Safavid, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> rulers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1867 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hosseinqoli-khan-bakhtiari">Hossein Qoli Khan</a> was recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> state as ilkhan, paramount chief, unifying the confederation; he was executed in 1882 on the order of Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zell-e-soltan">Zell-e Soltan</a>. The khans negotiated with British companies over the Lynch road and, after oil was found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjed-soleyman">Masjed Soleyman</a> in 1908, received a share in the oil companies working their lands. In 1909 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-qoli-khan-bakhtiari">Sardar As'ad II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najaf-qoli-khan-bakhtiari">Samsam al-Saltaneh</a> marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> and restored the constitution.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pahlavi-iran">Pahlavi Iran</a> disarmed the tribes, forced settlement and executed or imprisoned leading khans by 1934. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> remain a distinct people; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soraya-esfandiary-bakhtiary">Queen Soraya</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> was of Bakhtiari descent.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1700 CE – 1934 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.66%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1934 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hossein Qoli Khan, Sardar As'ad II, Samsam al-Saltaneh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bakhtiari Luri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bakhtiari, Bakhtiaris</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=bakhtiari-confederation" aria-label="Bakhtiari confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6093 1008 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bakhtiari confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6298 1144h0M6298 1144h0M6364 1269h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6413 1264h0"/><path clas